From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sproutboat <noreply@sproutboat.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:42:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] security: compiled code may not name the compiler's
 intrinsics (refuse.js)

`Porffor.c` puts its template text verbatim into the C output; Porffor.IR, Porffor.malloc, Porffor.link and the global
__Porffor_* and __<Builtin>_* functions (called by builtins with unchecked arguments) are as raw. All of them are
resolved statically, from identifiers, so the compiler now refuses the identifiers: `Porffor`, and any name of the
form __Name_x whose Name is a builtin namespace (__Porffor_malloc, __Array_prototype_join, __ecma262_ToString). A name of the same
shape with another Name is the program's own and passes (React's __COMPILER_RUNTIME and __SECRET_INTERNALS_..., zod's __zod_*,
rou3's __rou3_*, kysely's __kysely_*, partyserver's __unsafe_ensureInitialized, Rolldown's __toESMCache_*).

The check is on the AST right after parsing, so strings and comments never trigger it and unicode escapes are already
decoded. It runs on every module that is not the entry, the runtime, or the shared-prelude.js and anchor-ns.js beside
the entry (isUntrusted in modules.js; a data: module is untrusted), and on the code of every compile-time eval,
Function and vm source (their strings are parsed and compiled in). The error carries SB_INPUT_REFUSED.

The entry is trusted, so a standalone build (the author's own bundle is the entry) is unchanged. A compile that builds
the platform's own template (a worker.js holding the prelude) or develops the runtime passes --sb-allow-intrinsics.

It also refuses `node:ffi` (isNativeBuiltin in refuse.js, checked in `dep` in modules.js, so import, import(), require and
process.getBuiltinModule all fail): the module is raw native access, dlopen of any library and calls through function pointers, and its
runtime injects Porffor.c into the AST after the check above has run, so importing it bypassed the refusal of Porffor.dlopen. The same
trusted code and --sb-allow-intrinsics keep it. REFUSAL_LEVEL is 2. Other native-reaching builtins are not refused here.

Class: ours
Pass: refuseIntrinsics (refuse.js; modules.js, codegen.js, semantic.js)
---
 compiler/codegen.js  |  3 +-
 compiler/modules.js  | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 compiler/refuse.js   | 69 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 compiler/semantic.js |  3 +-
 4 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 compiler/refuse.js

